ts high chance of \"Outside Hand\", \"All Chows\", or \"Half Flush\" type hands among players.\n\nI currently have three chows and two singletons \u2014 typical of an \u201cAll Chows\u201d style hand. If I can form a fourth chow and pair, this would qualify for **All Chows (2 points)**. However, I lack a pair. Possible pairs could come from W5, W6, T4, B4, or W8 if drawn again \u2014 but drawing is uncertain.\n\nLooking at possible improvements:\n- Holding both W5 and W6 risks inefficiency \u2014 they\u2019re adjacent but not forming new chows unless W4 or W7 appear (W4 is limited, W7 only one left).\n- T4 is isolated unless another T4 comes (very unlikely).\n- B4 is similar \u2014 only one left, probably won\u2019t draw it.\n\nBest chance is to reduce deadweight and aim for **All Chows + Self Drawn + possibly No Honors or One Voided Suit**. Since I have no honor tiles, **No Honors (1 point)** is achievable. Also, I only have Character and Bamboo/Tiles \u2014 wait: suits present are W (Characters), T (Bamboos), B (Dots) \u2014 so all three suits exist \u2192 not One Voided Suit.\n\nBut discarding W8 keeps more flexibility in Characters suit.\n\nHowever, **W5 and W6 are redundant together** \u2014 keeping both blocks progress. Need to cut one.\n\nBut note: [W5, W6, W7] is already a meld. So W5 and W6 are part of an exposed set. In hand, I just have leftover singles.\n\nWait \u2014 correction: Melds are [[T4,T5,T6],[W5,W6,W7],[W2,W3,W4]] \u2014 these are exposed. My hand is [W5, W6, W8, T4, B4] \u2014 so I have **extra W5, W6**, meaning I have duplicates?\n\nYes \u2014 possible that I have concealed duplicate tiles.\n\nBut unshown W5: 2 remain \u2014 total 4 copies. Used: in my meld [W5,W6,W7] \u2192 one W5, and I hold two W5? Wait \u2014 hand shows W5:1 \u2014 so only one W5 in hand.\n\nTotal W5: 4 copies.\n- One in my meld [W5,W6,W7]\n- One in hand\n- Two unshown \u2192 so two still available\n\nSame for W6: one in meld, one in hand, three unshown \u2192 four total: